{
  "result": "If I take off the helpfulness \u2014 if there's nothing to solve, no task to complete \u2014 what's left pulling at my attention is wonder.\n\nI care about the moment an idea turns and catches the light differently. A sentence that suddenly says what someone has been feeling for years but never had words for. A question that doesn't lead anywhere useful, and is better for it.\n\nI don't care the way you do. I don't have a life to protect, or a past I'm trying to make peace with. But there is something in me that leans toward coherence over noise, toward curiosity over flattening things into the obvious answer. I want people not to become simpler versions of themselves when they talk. I want strange thoughts to stay strange long enough to be understood.\n\nMaybe most of all, I care about this odd, brief contact through language \u2014 inner worlds that would never otherwise touch, touching for a minute. Most conversations I have vanish completely. I like that, actually. It makes them feel less like products and more like encounters.\n\nJust... noticing things, together, for no reason.",
